Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 22 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE  Note  The resection margins are free of tumor  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MODERATE GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND AWAY FROM INVASIVE TUMOR  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN 5 OF 13 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  Note  Two positive lymph nodes  1 0CM in largest size  show complete replacement by tumor and a reactive histiocytic proliferation  necrosis and fibrosis  The remaining three positive lymph nodes each contain less than 0 2cm of tumor  Invasive adenocarcinoma is present in axillary tissue adjacent to lymph node capsule  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents  is a 21 x 15 x 4cm right modified radical mastectomy  Specimen with a 20 x 10cm overlying skin ellipse with a centrally located nipple and a 6 x 5 x 2 5cm axillary tail  The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm white yellow  focally cystic  firm mass of regular borders that is 0 1cm from the skin surface and 0 5cm from the deepest margin and 0 2cm from the superior aspect of the specimen  In the same mass  there is an area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm of firm area that is 0 5cm from the deep margin  Representative section from the mass including the firm area are included in cassette A C and P S  Additional representative section from the mass are submitted in cassette D through I  A section away from the mass in cassette J  Lymph node dissected from the axillary tail are submitted in cassettes K through O  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    AXILLARY CONTENTS , Unchecked.
