ally sectioned to reveal unremarkable tan yellow adipose tissue with diffuse hemorrhage  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Focally  the ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN ANTERIOR   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN MEDIAL   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN LATERAL   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION PART F  BREAST  LEFT  FINA  report_end  , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  07 MAY 96 at 13 14 CLINICAL DATA  New 1 0cm suspicious mass on mammography on May 3rd  Fine needle aspirate on May 6th was suspicious  Undergoing lumpectomy and axillary section                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  1   BIOPSY  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  2   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  3   BIOPSY  FAT AND SCANT UNREMARKABLE GLANDULAR TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN EIGHTEEN OF EIGHTEEN LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 MAY 96 at 13 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 MAY 96 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of breast with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined stellate  firm mass approximately 1 0cm in greatest dimension  adjacent to the superior medial inked margin  A representative section of this area is frozen as FX 1  and saved frozen  Representative sections of the medial half are submitted from superior to inferior  A through E  and representative sections of the lateral half are submitted superior to inferior in F through J  Labeled   2  right medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast tissue with short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen is inked black and the medial margin is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely from superior to inferior in K through O  Labeled   3  right superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of breast with a long suture designating the lateral  and a short suture designating the superior    anterior  margin  The specimen is inked black and the anterior flat surface    inferior aspect  is designated blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial and submitted in P through S  Labeled  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fat from which multiple lymph nodes are dissected  The nodes are submitted in T through W  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Horace C  Wu  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST  SPECIMEN  1 PART B  RIGHT BREAST  SPECIMEN  2  MEDIAL  PART C  RIGHT BREAST  SPECIMEN  3  SUPERIOR  PART D  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 38 CLINICAL DATA  Left modified radical mastectomy in a 45 year old female with a left breast mass which on mammogram was highly suggestive of carcinoma  FNA REMOVED_DATE showed isolated atypical cells  highly suggestive of carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  90    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   REMOVED_DATE CM IN SIZE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  THE RESECTION MARGINS ARE NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  2  TWENTY SEVEN OF TWENTY SEVEN LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 54                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 18     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Left breast and axillary contents  is a 25 x 21 x 5cm left mastectomy specimen with attached axillary contents and a 23 x 8cm ellipse of skin containing unremarkable 1cm in diameter nipple  No lesions on the skin surface are identified  The deep surface is a thin unremarkable fibrous tissue overlying adipose tissue and is inked  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm stellate firm white mass in the upper outer quadrant  5cm from the nipple and 2cm from the closest deep margin  A representative portion of the mass is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Another piece is saved for estrogen receptors  The remainder of the breast tissue is predominantly adipose tissue with thin strands of fibrous tissue  No additional suspicious lesions are seen  The attached 7 x 5 x 2cm portion of axillary tail contains unremarkable lymph nodes up to 1 3cm in size  Section Code  A D  tumor  E  closest deep margin  F G  surrounding breast tissue  H M  lymph nodes  N  nipple  Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  David Weissmann  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Lisa H  Lerner  MD                                                                             