Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 28 CLINICAL DATA  38 year old woman with left breast carcinoma now for re excision                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN FOURTEEN OF FOURTEEN LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 26                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm oriented piece of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm attached pink skin ellipse with a 1 7cm linear scar  There is a long stitch marking lateral and a short stitch marking superior  The entire specimen is inked black with the medial margin overinked green and the inferior margin overinked orange  The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm probable biopsy cavity surrounded by fibrosis  Adjacent to the cavity  superiorly  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm white stellate mass  The mass extends anteriorly abutting the anterior margin  The mass is entirely submitted in cassettes A F with bisected sections in B C and E F  Representative sections of biopsy cavity are submitted entirely from cassettes G I from medial to lateral  A representative section of uninvolved breast parenchyma is taken from the medial aspect of the specimen and submitted in cassette J  A representative section of the dense fibrous tissue is frozen as FX  2 and submitted in cassette K  The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes several of which are found ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The nodes are submitted in toto in cassettes L P except for cassette O which a bisected node  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel lymph node  1  813   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow soft fatty lymph node which is bisected and frozen entirely as FX 1 and submitted in cassette Q  Resident  PAULA ARNELL  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  1   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST  LEFT  DEEP MARGIN   DENSE FIBROSIS  NO TUMOR SEEN  O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURG   ACC 457 REPORTS TO  Sarah P Thayer  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 08 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal mammogram left breast  Two lesions are noted in A and B                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  A   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  40    GRADE REMOVED_DATE EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Several microcalcifications are seen in slide A and E  No lymphatic or vascular invasion identifed  This tumor measures 1 1cm in diameter  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  B   INFILTRATING  80   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  20    GRADE REMOVED_DATE EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Microcalcifications are seen in slide M  No lymphatic or vascular invascular invasion  The tumor measures 0 8cm in diameter  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  BOTH SPECIMENS   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  A  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibronodular fibrous tissue with localizing wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a stellate firm white lesion with central hemorrhagic focus measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm extending to the inked margin  Specimen is submitted in cassettes A through F  nodule in A   C  representative sections in cassettes D  E  and F  Representative section of nodule frozen and saved  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  B  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fatty fibrous tissue with localizing wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm  white nodule   1  approximately 1cm from inked margin  and a separate irregular white lesion   2  measuring 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm at the margin  Nodule in cassette G  second irregular lesion  2 in cassettes H and I  Representative sections in J through N  Representative section of rounded nodule  1 saved frozen  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST SPECIMEN A   SMALL CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST SPECIMEN B   SMALL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST LESION SPECIMEN A  B   report_end  , Unchecked.
