ls stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast tissue excision  The specimen is oriented  short stitch designates superior  long stitch designates lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  On cross sectioning  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined  white gray firm gritty mass  This mass focally abuts the posterior margin  is 0 1cm from the closest inferior margin 1 0cm from anterior margin  1 5cm from medial margin  2 5cm from lateral margin and 3 5cm from superior margin  Located 0 5cm away from the mass  superior aspect from mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm cystic cavity with smooth inner tan pink inner lining which could correspond to previous biopsy site  The remaining breast parenchyma is approximately 50  fibrous tissue and 50  adipose tissue  The fibrous tissue is ill defined and has several small cystic structures  The specimen is submitted as follows  A D  representative sections of the mass with closest margins  E   cystic cavity and its relation to the mass  F H  representative sections of the fibrous tissue away from the mass  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  inferior half of cavity  shave margins  are two irregular portions of f