 labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and   right axillary sentinel nodes   are 2 pieces of yellow  fibroadipose tissue  5  x 3 x 2cm and 3 x 3 x 0 7cm  dissected to reveal 2 lymph nodes  3 x 2 x 1cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The 0 9cm lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen  as FX 1  now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The 3cm lymph node is serially sectioned and  entirely frozen as FX 1A  FX 1B  FX 1C  FX 1D  which are now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively  The remaining fibroadipose tissue present in the  container is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast and skin   is  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  simple mastectomy specimen with a short suture  designating the superior margin and a long suture designating the lateral  margin  per the surgeon  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 2cm ellipse of skin appears  unremarkable  The nipple and areola appear unremarkable  The anterior margin  is inked blue  the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen contains a  3 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  tan pink  focally yellow  ill defined  rubbery mass in the  upper outer quadrant  in approximately 10 o clock position  which extends to  1 9cm from the posterior margin and 2 0cm from the anterior margin  A clip  is not identified  The surrounding tissue consists of tan yellow to pink white  lobulated  focally granular fibrofatty breast tissue  and displays associated  hemorrhage and fat necrosis  Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral  tissue     Additionally received in the same container are 2 irregularly  tan white   unremarkable portions of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm   REMOVED_DATE x 9 2cm  both  with minimal attached fibrofatty breast tissue  Representative sections are  submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as labeled      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative mas