hat failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 03     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast wire  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire in place  A x ray film accompanies the specimen  The tissue is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 4cm firm  tan  stellate area 0 1cm from the closest inked margin  No frozen section done  Submitted entirely in cassettes A through D  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   LEFT  BREAST MASS  LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
