aining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 96 at 09 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm portion of fibrofatty tissue and an accompanying radiograph  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  stellate  ill defined  firm  white area which is at the margin  No frozen is performed  The specimen is submitted entirely with the stellate region in cassettes A through E  remaining tissue is submitted entirely in cassette F  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST MASS   FIRM TISSUE SUSPICIOUS FOR MALIGNANCY  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST SKIN  LEFT  PART B  BREAST AND CALCIFICATION  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
