ative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast and axillary nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm tan white skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of axillary fat pad  There is a 1 5cm raised nipple  Adjacent to the nipple areolar complex is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm yellow purple discolored area  The specimen is oriented by the axillary tail and there is one long suture on the superior aspect  Sectioning through the specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm firm  focally gritty  gray white to yellow fatty mass  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hemorrhagic focus within this mass  which is presumed to be the previous site of biopsy  This firm mass is within 0 3cm of the deep margin  0 7cm of the skin surface  and appears to abut the inferior margin  Sectioning through the remaining breast reveals predominately yellow fatty tissue with a small amount of gray white fibrous tissue and no other grossly appreciated masses  Several lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  ranging in size from 0 6cm to 2 1cm in greatest dimension and a representative section of each lymph node is submitted  SECTION CODE  A C  Firm  gray white mass to the deep margin  D   Mass to inferior margin  E F  Sections from area of hemorrhage within mass  G   Skin  H K  Lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of adipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 6cm to 1 5cm in greatest dimensions  The cut surfaces of the lymph nodes are tan to gray white  Representative sections are submitted in Cassettes L N  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Edi Brogi  M D   PhD  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
