ns  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistently shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 17 34     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  51 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  107 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received on ice  labeled  Left breast mass   is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm  gritty  ill defined nodule approaching to within 0 3cm of the nearest margin  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue is submitted for Estrogen receptors and BRDU studies  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in A through K  Resident  Robert F  Cheek  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Steven Ralph Levisohn  M D  David William Rattner  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 09 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE RESECTION MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  NOTE  No definitive lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 49 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor rpotein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm stellate  firm  white lesion abutting the inked margin  Submitted entirely in A through E  Gross Description by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Resident  Frank P  Fechner  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
