 necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right mastectomy and axillary contents is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right mastectomy specimen with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail  with a short stitch designating superior  now redesignated as 12 o clock  and a long stitch designating axillary contents  The specimen is surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm tan white skin ellipse with an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple that comes to within 1 4cm of the 5 o clock margin  Located 3 4cm superior lateral to the nipple is a 1 7cm well healed  firm  linear scar  3 8cm from the 12 o clock margin  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm tan  firm  hemorrhagic  ill defined mass that comes to within 2 3cm from the black inked deep margin and 2 2cm from the skin surface  Subjacent to the surface scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm area of calcifications  and comes to within 4 5cm from the mass  Located 6 5cm superior lateral to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm area of calcifications that abut the anterior blue inked surface and comes to within 0 3cm of the posterior black inked surface  The remainder of the tissue is predominantly tan yellow  unremarkable fatty tissues admixed with a scant amount of tan white fibrous tissue  Multiple tan  rubbery lymph nodes are identified in the axillary fat  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A C  Tumor to deep margin  D  Tumor  E  Uninvolved tissue medial to tumor  F  Uninvolved tissue  lateral to tumor  G H  Calcifications  subjacent to scar  I  Calcifications lateral to mass  J  Four whole lymph nodes  K  Two whole lymph node  bisected  L  One lymph node bisected  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of tan yellow  nodular  lobulated fatty tissue  from which three  tan  rubbery lymph nodes are identified  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  M  Two whole lymph nodes  N  One whole lymph node bisected  Gross Description by  BRAD MOSBURG Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  FCK                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART B  BREAST RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 54 CLINICAL DATA  53 year old female with breast silicone implant  status post left breast biopsy in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   intraductal carcinoma   and right breast biopsy in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   fibrocystic changes   now with new left and right mammographic signs and palpable left axillary nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  0 5 CM   50   EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED MARGIN  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  50   AT AN INKED MARGIN  3  EXTENSIVE SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  4  FIBROADENOMA  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Evaluation of the adequacy of margins is difficult because of the nature of the tumor and the degree of the cautery changes  Neither lymphatic nor blood vessel invasion are seen  The nodule that was frozen is a fibroadenoma  no cancer cells are present in the frozen section tissue  Slides from the right side excision were also reviewed by Drs  Frederick Koerner and Dennis Sgroi  who agree with the diagnosis  Immunostains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be done and reported as an addendum  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   BIOPSY FOR FROZEN SECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Tumor cells in the lymph node are more anaplastic than those in the breast primary  but the cytoarchitectural features  including signet ring cells  targetoid cells and histiocytoid cells  are consistent with a carcinoma of lobular type  Intracytoplasmic mucin is demonstrated in rare cells on special stains  particularly the Alcian Blue and PAS stains   supporting a diagnosis of adenocarcinoma  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA WITHIN 4 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  1  BIOPSY SITE  WITH HEMORRHAGE  HISTIOCYTIC REACTION  FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  AND SUTURE GRANULOMAS  2  EXTENSIVE SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS AND FOCAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 7 OF 7 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  DESIGNATED  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY NODE    BIOPSY  AUTOLYZED LYMPH NODE AND ADJACENT SUTURE FRAGMENT  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 52 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      ELECTRON MICROSCOPY Addendum          ELECTRON MICROSCOPY    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The neoplastic cells are large  oval and polygonal  Their surface is covered with multiple filopodia  some of which may be true villi  Desmosomes and intermediate junctions  but no definite tight junctions  are found along lines of contact between cells  The cytoplasm is filled with many different organelles  but the most diagnostic structures are the bundles of filaments consistent with tonofibrils and squamous differentiation  either primary or metaplastic  Added by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 09     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimen parts are received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and the following  Labeled  Right breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  yellow  semifirm piece of fatty breast tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan skin ellipse  and a localizing wire in place  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm in diameter  well defined  semifirm nodule adjacent to the hook of the wire and located 0 2cm from the deep inked margin  A representative section of this nodule is frozen as FX 1 and submitted in A  The remainder of the nodule is submitted in B D  The ends and body of the skin ellipse are submitted in E   F  respectively  the other tissue in G K  Labeled  Right axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan  semifirm lymph node  sectioned perpendicular to the long axis to reveal a tan  fleshy cut surface  No discrete lesions are noted  A representative section is frozen as FX 2  and saved frozen  Half of the remaining tissue is fixed in formalin overnight  and now submitted in L O  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in P Q  following B 5 fixation  A portion of tissue is kept for possible electron microscopy   TIE   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are four more parts  These parts sat in an operating room refrigerator for two days before being sent to pathology  according to a notation on the requisition  Labeled  left breast re excision  is an ellipse of skin REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm with central healed scar  Underlying the skin ellipse is a fragment of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  A long suture designates the 12 o clock position  a short suture designates the 9 o clock position  the 3 o clock side is inked yellow on black  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted in cassettes in AA through ZZ  from 12 o clock to 6 o clock  Labeled  re excision axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes  About twelve possible lymph nodes are dissected out  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  the largest lymph nodes are sectioned and submitted in AAA CCC  the smaller lymph node fragments in DDD  Labeled  additional axillary node  is a white yellow fragment of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Within this tissue is a hard nodule REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm entirely submitted in EEE  Labeled with patient s name and unit number only is a an aggregate of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  The material contains multiple lymph nodes  approximately 11  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  the largest lymph nodes are sectioned and submitted in FFF HHH  the smaller lymph nodes are submitted entirely in III   GOR  Gross Description by  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  FIBROADENOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  METASTATIC ANAPLASTIC TUMOR CELL  O R  Resident  Horace C  Wu  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Alik Farber  M D  Mark Atkinson Vangorder  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  BIOPSY FOR FROZEN PART C  RIGHT AXILLARY DISSECTION PART D  LEFT BREAST RE EXCISION PART E  LEFT AXILLARY DISSECTION PART F  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY NODE , Unchecked.
