sults of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of breast tissue with localization needle and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal lumpy  firm to rubbery  white and off yellow breast tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through J  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION , Checked.
