Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 55 CLINICAL DATA  Re excision of intraductal  multifocal carcinoma in situ                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  ONE FOCUS FIVE MILLIMETERS IN DIAMETER  SLIDE L  AND ABUTTING INKED MARGIN AT ONE POINT  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENSIVE  INVOLVING APPROXIMATELY TWO THIRDS OF SLIDES  AND PRESENT AT INKED MARGIN  NOTE  Infiltrating ductal carcinoma represents approximately 2  of the tumor  The tissue used for frozen section does not contain carcinoma  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH MICROCYSTS  4  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  5  SURGICAL EXCISION SITE  WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION TO BIREFRINGENT MATERIAL  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 39                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  tan  yellow  fibrofatty mass with 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin attached  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm biopsy cavity with surrounding ill defined white to tan tissue  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in A  the remainder of tissue is submitted in B through N  Resident  FANG FANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   REACTIVE FIBROSIS  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Carlos Fernandez del castillo  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
