Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a 20 x 20 x 4 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  an axillary tail measuring 11 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  and a strip of muscle measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The nipple is inverted with areas of nodularity around it  and there are two pink red bruises measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in greatest dimension over the skin  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned into twelve slices from medial to lateral  and reveals a firm stellate mass  identified by a clip  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The mass is found towards the middle of the specimen in slices seven and eight  The closest deep margin is 3 5cm from the mass  and 2 5cm from the skin  One arm of the stellate mass extends inferiorly and towards the axillary tail forming a firm nodularity but no discrete mass  and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and is found in slices eight and nine  This nodularity is 4 0cm from the black ink  There is a second  ill defined  stellate  firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  which abuts the nipple and is found in slices five and six  This area is 3 0cm medial to the stellate mass identified by the clip and is 4 0cm from the black ink  The rest of the breast tissue consists of grossly unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is submitted as follows  A  Portion of stellate mass and closest black inked margin  B D  Further representative sections of the stellate mass  E  Nipple with mass abutting nipple  F and G  Further representative sections of lesion beneath nipple  H I  Representative sections of nodularity extending inferiorly and medially from scar  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail and submitted individually in cassettes J P  A large  possibly matted lymph node bisected and submitted in cassette Q and R  One lymph node bisected and now in S T  U  Six small lymph nodes submitted entirely  Most of the lymph nodes contain necrotic pasty material  V W  Grossly unremarkable breast tissue  NOTE  The tumor extensively involves lymphatic vessels  Definite stromal invasion is not seen  but micro invasion cannot be completely excluded  The margin of the specimen appears free of tumor  Resident  SHABIN NANJI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 04 CLINICAL DATA  Breast cancer by core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MEASURED FROM SLIDE D   GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHATIC OR BLOOD VASCULAR INVASION  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  PREDOMINATING NEAR THE INVASIVE TUMOR  BUT ALSO EXTENDING AWAY  AND PRESENT AS TWO FOCI IN A SECTION NOT CONTAINING INVASIVE TUMOR  E   3  HEALING CORE BIOPSY SITE  4  ADJACENT NODULE OF DENSELY SCLEROTIC BREAST  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION OF ADDITIONAL MARGIN  DENSE SCLEROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 22 33                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lesion   is an REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast fragment with a long stitch designating superior aspects and a short stitch designating inferior aspects and a wire designating the antero lateral aspects  The specimen is inked  then sectioned along the needle localization wire to reveal an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm white mass  coming to within than less than 0 1cm of the anteromedial resection margin  This is frozen as FX  1 and FX  2  and resubmitted in cassettes A and B  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  and  left breast margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch indicating the former closest margin  opposite to which is the new margin  this is inked black and a representative radial section is frozen as FX  3 and now resubmitted in C  The remainder of the specimen is inked in blue where the stitch is and black  on the opposite side  sectioned and submitted serially  Further identified as left axillary contents is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of fatty  nodular tissue  with a suture designating the highest node  Section Code  D E  additional sections of main fragment through antero medial aspects adjacent to tip of needle  Further sections reveal a tan  fibrous area located deep  medially REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  F  representative sections through tan  fibrous area of main fragment  G O  remainder of  margin  specimen serially submitted P  highest node Q V  lymph nodes  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 AND  2   LEFT BREAST LESION   INVASIVE DUCTAL AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  TUMOR PRESENT AT ANTERIOR MEDIAL INKED MARGINS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  3   LEFT BREAST MARGIN   NO TUMOR IS SEEN IN PERPENDICULAR SECTIONS FROM NEW MARGIN  O R  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  LESION PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
