 lateral aspect  A tan skin ellipse is present anteriorly which measures REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm areola with nipple  A faint well healed linear scar measuring 1 8cm is present at the skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm ill defined  firm  stellate scar within the breast parenchyma subjacent to the medial end of the skin ellipse  The scar extends to the deep resection margin along a broad front  No residual tumor is grossly identified  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed predominantly of white tan fibrotic soft tissue  marbled with a small amount of yellow fatty tissue  Within the parenchyma  away from the scar  is a rubbery  well circumscribed solid and cystic mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in greatest dimensions  This mass has a smooth tan white homogeneous cut surface in the solid areas  The cystic areas have a smooth lining and are filled with a straw colored clear fluid  This mass extends to within 0 2cm of the deep resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is remarkable only for focal fibrocystic change  The tissue is dissected and examined for lymph nodes but none are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code  A J  Scar to deep margin  scar is submitted entirely   K M  Representative sections of rubbery mas  N O  Uninvolved parenchyma  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Checked.
