e predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 95 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm mass  within 0 4cm of the closest resection margin  The remaining tissue is unremarkable  Three sections from the nodule including surrounding margin are submitted in cassettes A through C  a section 2 0cm away from the nodule is submitted in cassette D  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION  REMOVED_DATE CM NODULE THAT IS SUGGESTIVE OF INVASIVE TUMOR  WITH SUSPICIOUS CELLS ON TOUCH PREPORATION  DIAGNOSIS DEFERRED TO FINAL HISTOLOGICAL SECTIONS  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
