 this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 04     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a yellow  irregular segment of fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen is inked and dissected to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm mass approximately 1 0cm from the posterior margin  No frozen section done  Dr  Gadd simply wanted to know where the closest margin is  Section code  A  lesion and anterior margin B  lesion and posterior margin C  lesion and deep margin DandE representative sections of the lesion Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right axillary contents  levels 1 and 2  is a piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Lymph nodes are bissected and submitted in cassettes F I  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Najmosama Nikrui  M D  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Diane R Fingold  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 54 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma with lumpectomy 7 years ago                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is very poorly circumscribed and is REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in cross section  as measured from the slides  It focally extends to within less than 1mm of the resection margin in several foci  A circumscribed nodule of tumor associated with a small rim of lymphocytes is also present  It is not possible to determine if this is a separate tumor nodule  or a small lymph node completely replaced by carcinoma  Extensive lymphatic permeation is present  There is no evidence of an in situ component  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 49                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 02     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum   