Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 25 CLINICAL DATA  NONE                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOCAL  HIGH GRADE  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  Note  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  ill defined  stellate  white  firm mass with focally yellow discoloration and a gritty cut surface  extending 0 1cm from the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in A  the remainder of the mass is submitted in B D  Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
