ts  Sectioning reveals unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  some of which is focally dense  with fibrous tissue radiating to all margins  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The metal clip adjacent to the localization wire is identified  The  second clip at benign fibroadenoma  is a not identified  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as follows  A  Area identified by wire  anterior  posterior  inferior margins  B  Area identified by wire  posterior and inferior margins  C  Area identified by wire  posterior and superior margins  D  Area identified by wire  anterior  posterior  inferior margins  E  Area identified by wire  posterior and inferior margins  F  Area identified by clip  anterior  posterior  superior margins    second clip area  G  Area identified by clip  anterior and posterior margins  H  Area identified by clip  anterior  posterior  inferior margins  I  Area identified by clip  anterior margin  J  Area identified by clip  posterior and inferior margins  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional lateral margins  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan yellow  focally cauterized fibrofatty tissue  A suture designates the surface furthest from the tumor  The sutured aspect of the specimen is black inked and the opposing aspect is blue inked  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes K O  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary lymph nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of tan yellow  lobular fibroadipose tissue within which multiple tan lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm are identified  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  P  2 whole lymph nodes  Q  3 whole lymph nodes  R  1 whole possible lymph node  S  1 lymph node bisected  T  1 lymph node bisected  U  1 lymph node bisected  V W  1 lymph node bisected  X Y  1 lymph node bisec