Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 19 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING SKELETAL MUSCLE AND EXTENDING TO THE DEEP MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  Note  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA OCCUPYING 3 OF 10 LYMPH NODES AND INVADING AXILLARY SOFT TISSUE  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SEPARATELY SUBMITTED   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm modified radial mastectomy specimen  that includes a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm attached axillary tail  and overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm skin ellipse containing a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm nipple areola complex  located 0 8cm from the inferior skin margin  Extending superomedially from the nipple a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm erythematous ulcer is identified with a central 1 3cm ulceration and peripheral  firm  red  slightly raised edges  extending to within 1 2cm from the closest skin resection margin  superomedially   The posterior  deep margin  contains a palpable firmness with overlying puckering of the adipose tissue  located 4 0cm from the superior soft tissue margin  and 5 0cm both the medial and inferior soft tissue margin  Sectioning through this area reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  tan white  firm  stellate mass that extends to the deep margin in the area of overlying puckered firmness  extends to the skin in the area of overlying ulceration  and to within 1 5cm of the closest soft tissue resection margin  superomedial   Apart from the mass  two other tan white  firm  stellate masses are identified  The first  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  is located 1 8cm inferior to the main mass  1 5cm from the closest deep resection margin  and 4 0cm from the inferior resection margin  The second mass measures REMOVED_DATE x0 5 x 0 8cm  is located 0 5cm from the main mass  1 7cm from the deep resection margin  and 2 5cm from the inferior soft tissue resection margin  In addition  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  ill defined  firm to rubbery  fibrous area is identified inferolaterally from the main mass  located 3 0cm from the inferior soft tissue resection margin and 1 8cm from the deep resection margin  Apart from the aforementioned abnormal areas  the remaining breast parenchyma is composed to yellow  lobulated  soft adipose tissue  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 7cm in greatest dimension  The cut surfaces  range from tan brown and soft to firm and tan white  Submitted in M through Q  SECTION CODE A  Nipple with mass  B  Skin with mass  C F  Mass with deep resection margin  G  Tumor  representative  H  Smaller mass  1  I  Smaller mass  2  J L  Fibrous area  M Q  Lymph nodes  Labeled  left axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan whiter firm lymph node  bisected and entirely submitted in R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  PART A  LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE   report_end  , Unchecked.
