Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 16 CLINICAL DATA  History of left breast carcinoma  status post reconstruction                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  APOCRINE TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is not seen  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  APOCRINE TYPE INVOLVING A MACROCYST  HIGH GRADE  ARISING IN ASSOCIATION WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of breast tissue with needle  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm white tan mass with a 1 0cm central cystic area  A representative section of tumor is frozen as fx 1 and saved frozen  The remaining tumor is submitted in cassettes A D with additional representative sections of normal breast in cassette E F  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  WITH APOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION , Unchecked.
