Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 48 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA FORMING MANY SEPARATE NODULES THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN MANY FOCI  IN SITU CARCINOMA WITH FEATURES OF BOTH LOBULAR AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SCATTERED SMALL FOCI THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN AND FOCALLY AT THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  Note  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   FIBROSIS  SEE NOTE  Note  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 97 at 14 42     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal predominantly fibrous cut surface without distinct mass lesions  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  The remainder is entirely submitted in cassettes A through D  Labeled  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm soft tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous and fatty cut surfaces  without distinct mass lesion  A representative section is frozen as FX  2  and submitted in J  The reminder of the specimen is entirely submitted in E through I  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT BREAST MASS  DENSE FIBROSIS  NO INVASIVE CARCINOMA SEEN  O R  Resident  Navneet Narula  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
