Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 09 CLINICAL DATA  36 year old female with left breast biopsy in REMOVED_MONTH 29   REMOVED_CASE_ID  done at Lawerence Hospital showing invasive ductal cancer  Grade 3 extensively invading lymphatic vessels and extending to less than 0 1cm from the margin of the specimen  No blood vessel invasion seen                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   SEVERAL SCATTERED FOCI MEASURING REMOVED_DATE CM IN AGGREGATE  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  FIBROSIS  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR SURGERY  NOTE  Blood vascular invasion is not seen  The margins are free of tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY DISSECTION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TEN OF TEN LYMPH NODES  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE INTRAOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL TISSUE  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of unremarkable breast  all submitted in cassettes A through K  Representative section is frozen as FX 1 and kept frozen and will be sent to Cox 5  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm skin ellipse containing a 3 0cm  well healed scar and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm unremarkable nipple  Also attached to the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail  No biopsy cavity is identified  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  focally red and focally pink area which extends to 1 5cm of the closest deep inked margin  The rest of the breast parenchyma is focally white and focally yellow and grossly unremarkable  Section code  L  representative section of mass in relationship to deep inked margin M Q  additional representative sections of mass R T  biopsy cavity U V  representative section of breast parenchyma away from mass W  representative section of nipple Eleven lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm is present in axillary tail  sectioned to reveal tan to pink cut surface  Representative sections submitted in cassettes X through AA  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast tissue  is an aggregate of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  sectioned to reveal mostly unremarkable fat  Representative portions submitted in cassettes BB CC  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITIES RECOGNIZED  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  G  Gregory Gallico III  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL TISSUE , Unchecked.
