Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Omer Yilmaz  M D   Ph D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Rajni V Mandal  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Devon Gimbel  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Locally advanced triple negative invasive ductal carcinoma of the left breast  status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST AND AXILLARY TISSUE  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  SLIGHT FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  CELLULAR CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH NEOADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT  NO RESIDUAL CARCINOMA CELLS ARE IDENTIFIED WITHIN THE BREAST PARENCHYMA  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITHIN 4 OF 4 NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  All of the candidate lymph nodes that are dissected from the modified radical mastectomy specimen and from the separately submitted left axillary tissue specimen have the appearance of fibroinflammatory nodules containing histiocytes  plasma cells  necrotic cellular material and focal hemosiderin deposits  Very rare isolated viable appearing tumor cells are identified in these nodules  Although the number of residual tumor cells is very small  the appearance is consistent with lymph nodes that may have been largely or completely replaced by tumor before chemotherapy treatment  Because of scarring  the presence or absence of extranodal extension cannot be assessed  No residual tumor cells are identified within the breast parenchyma  which has been extensively sampled for microscopic examination  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY  ADDITIONAL   REGIONAL DISSECTION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITHIN 5 OF 5 NODES  SEE NOTE ABOVE  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  SLIGHT FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY WITHIN THE BREAST  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE INCLUDED LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   315   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right sentinel node  315   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibrofatty soft tissue  with one REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm lymph node that is frozen entirely as FX 1 and is now submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right simple mastectomy   is a 27 x 18 x 5cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen  with a short stitch designating the superior and a long stitch designating the lateral margins  The anterior surface contains a 23 x 10 5cm light brown skin ellipse with a 3 5cm in diameter areola and a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple  which are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominantly tan yellow  lobulated cut surface interspersed with moderate fibrous tissue  No discrete mass or lesion is appreciated  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from central quadrant  Received f