Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 14 CLINICAL DATA  51 year old with abnormal mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT BREAST    BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES AND WITH FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 25                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm piece of yellow red  irregular  firm to hard tissue with a localizing wire in place and accompaying X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined tan white hard lesion  grossly abutting a resection margin  Portion is frozen as FX 1  now in A   Entirely in A E  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO AN INKED SURFACE  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY , Unchecked.
