en we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 97 at 17 03     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment with a suture designating the biopsy cavity margin  The margin is inked black and the remainder of the specimen is inked blue  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm hard  tan pink  well circumscribed mass  0 4cm from the biopsy cavity margin and 0 9cm from the other resection margin  The remainder of the specimen is unremarkable  Section code  AandB mass and closest margin CandD uninvolved breast tissue  representative sections Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue fragment with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse  The cut surface reveals fibrocystic changes with no grossly evident mass  Section code  E K  breast tissue with radiographic evidence of microcalcification  representative sections L Z  breast parenchyma  representative sections Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE  RESECTION MARGIN FREE OF TUMOR  FROZEN SECTION GROSS DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT BREAST  NO IDENTIFIABLE TUMOR SEEN  O R  Resident  Navneet Narula  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SPECIMEN  1 PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SPECIMEN  2   report_end  , Checked.
