Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  29 AUG 94 at 13 08 CLINICAL DATA  Obvious carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITH MUCIN PRODUCTION  2 CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  GRADE REMOVED_DATE   95   WITH METASTASIS IN ONE OF 26 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE   5     FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  MICROCALCIFICATION  APOCRINE METAPLASIA AND INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  NOTE  The tumor secretes abundant mucin and has squamous metaplasia in the axillary nodal metastasis  Vascular invasion is not identified  The resection margins are free of tumor  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  LYMPH NODE  LEFT  NEAR LATISSIMUS DORSI   EXCISION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY   SINUS HISTIOCYTOSIS AND FOLLICULAR HYPERPLASIA  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two specimens  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x0 5 x 0 3cm piece of hard  white tissue with a small amount adherent fat  All frozen as FX 1 and submitted in A  Labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm modified radical mastectomy with an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The 2 0cm in average diameter nipple is inverted  Lateral to the areolar is a 3 0cm recently sutured incision  At the base of the recent biopsy cavity is a firm  white to tan  gritty nodule  2 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8  which is variably REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm from the deep resection margin  The nodule is 3 0cm from the superior inferior margins  Medial to the biopsy site and adjacent to the deep resection margin the parenchyma is white  rubbery  with multiple cystic spaces  ranging in diameter from less than 0 1cm up to 0 3cm  This parenchyma covers and expands approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and terminates 2 0cm from the medial resection margin  The parenchyma between the previous identified nodule and axillary tail is composed entirely of fibroadipose tissue  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as FX 2 and saved frozen  The attached axillary tail is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm from which multiple lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely  In the adipose tissue at axillary tail nearest the breast is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm white nodule  SECTION CODE  B E  breast nodule  br report_end  , Unchecked.
