Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 30 CLINICAL DATA  Patient with history of lymphoma on FNA of breast nodule                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  HIGH GRADE B CELL LYMPHOMA  NOTE  The lymphoma is composed of medium sized cells with round to irregular nuclei and a moderate amount of cytoplasm  The cells are smaller than those of typical large cell lymphoma and in areas resemble those of Burkitt like lymphoma  However the mitotic rate  while high  is less than typical Burkitt like lymphoma and  starry sky  histiocytes are not prominent  In addition  the Ki67 proliferation marker is positive in 50 70  of tumor cells  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  04 MAY 98 at 13 56                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibody to B lineage  antigen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are negative for antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to T lineage associated antigens  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of cells scattered within the tissue  The cells are also positive for Ki 67 in approximately 50 70  of the cells  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of B cell lymphoma  Added by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 98 at 18 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast nodule   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate of tan pink to brown soft tissue  one half submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   now in cassette A  The remainder is submitted in cassette B  Gross Description by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Mark J Ott  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 24 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable nodules at 3 o clock on the right  calcium at 12 o clock on the right      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  AMENDED CLINICAL HISTORY Revised by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Revised on 10 AUG 98 at 11 47                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  TISSUE CALCIFICATIONS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  TWO SEPARATE FOCI SPANNING REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY PRESENT AT INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT  BREAST NODULE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOCALLY PRESENT AT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE CLOSEST RESECTION MARGIN  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Edited by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 16 10 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   Tissue calcifications    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast tissue calcification  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm unoriented fibroadipose breast tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma  submitted entirely in A through F  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 6cm fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in G and H  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST NODULE   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  TISSUE CALCIFICATIONS    EXCISIONAL PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  BREAST NODULE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 34 CLINICAL DATA  Malignancy on core biopsy of right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INFERIOR RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE   Note  Lymphatic vessel or vascular invasion is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT INFERIOR AND LATERAL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Immunohistochemical studies for keratin will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 41                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     Immunohistochemical stains for keratin show no positive cells in the lymph nodes  Added by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 12     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localization wire  short stitch designating superior margin which is inked in black  long stitch designating lateral margin which is inked in blue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm  white mass with peripheral retraction located 0 2cm from the inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J with mass in G and H  No frozen section done  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are three parts  Labeled  additional inferior and lateral margin  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 5cm fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked entirely in black  The superior margin is overlaid with blue  inferior is overlaid with red  lateral margin is overlaid with yellow and the anterior is overlaid with green  Sectioning to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely from lateral to medial in cassettes K through M  Labeled  final shaved margin  is an unoriented fragment of fatty adipose tissue measuring 3 x 3 x 0 5cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma except focal hemorrhagic areas  Entirely submitted in cassettes N through Q  Labeled  right axillary content  is a 6 x 5 x 2cm fatty adipose tissue  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely in cassettes R through T  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  FIRM  WHITE NODULE SUGGESTIVE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LOCATED LESS THAN 1 MM FROM INKED INFERIOR MARGIN  NOT FROZEN  O R  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Barbara Joyce Nath  M D  David Nathan Helman  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR   LATERAL    EXCISIONAL BI PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISIONAL B PART D  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION , Unchecked.
