ic foci of ductal carcinoma in situ  grade 3  focally present at the  final margin     F  BREAST EXCISION  LEFT LATERAL FINAL MARGIN     No malignancy identified     G  BREAST EXCISION  LEFT DEEP FINAL MARGIN     Flat epithelial atypia       Note  The resection margins of the specimens were inked and microscopically  evaluated          Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       PROCEDURES ADDENDA    Hormone Receptor Quantitation  Ordered Date  REMOVED_DATE    A  BREAST EXCISION  LEFT   Block tested   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   Some ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor  protein     B  BREAST EXCISION  RIGHT   Block tested   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor  protein     Note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive  nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows     The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained     Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained     Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained     The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained                      Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 16 37       CLINICAL HISTORY  Ductal carcinoma in situ     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST EXCISION  LEFT  B  BREAST EXCISION  RIGHT  C  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT ANTERIOR  D  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT SUPERIOR  E  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT MEDIAL  F  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT LATERAL  G  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT DEEP    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh ar