Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  MS 11  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  MS 11  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit    Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1  Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D   Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D              Addended Report                Reason for Amendment  1  Additional Diagnostic Information  Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results  Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH   Results  CLINICAL DATA   Right breast cancer  positive axillary lymph node  Status post cores   IDC   grade REMOVED_DATE  ER positive  PR positive  Her2 negative  Right breast cancer with  axillary lymph node  right modified mastectomy  left simple mastectomy       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     AMENDMENT NOTE  This case is amended because the tumor grade had not been  transcribed in the initial report  On review  the invasive carcinoma in the  breast shows grade 2 foci as well as grade 3 areas  the latter ones  predominating   Both areas show high grade nuclear features and a lack of  tubule formation  but the grade 3 areas show more copious cytoplasm and a  higher mitotic rate  Identical features are seen in the nodal metastases  The  results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone  receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ  hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an  addendum both for the primary tumor  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and one of the nodal metastases    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID         BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITHIN 11 OF 21 LYMPH NODES  11 21   SEE TABLE  2     TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA    