Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 38 CLINICAL DATA  History of DCIS                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 34                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm yellow tan irregular  fatty soft tissue specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm skin ellipse and a 3 5cm x 0 1cm central healed incision scar  The long axis of the specimen and skin ellipse is on the transverse plane and the skin ellipse is attached on the medial half of the soft tissue specimen  The entire soft tissue margin is inked black and the superior half is overinked blue  The inferior margin is overinked yellow and the deep margin is left black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic cavity surrounded by several focal areas of white firm areas  Grossly the cavity is 0 8cm from the lateral suture and closest it gets to the deep margin is 0 3cm  The rest of the specimen has no gross lesions  Section code  A D  Biopsy cavity  lateral to medial E  Soft tissue adjacent and medial to the cavity F  Representative section through the skin ellipse G  Representative section adjacent lateral to the cavity  H I  Lateral margin radial sections  Resident  TAN A  INCE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION   report_end  , Unch