Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  26 AUG 97 at 13 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW TO INTERMEDIATE GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND TO SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  3  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  4  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion are not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 AUG 97 at 16 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast with needle and specimen X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a nodular  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  white  rubbery mass which grossly abuts inked margins  The nodule was bisected and submitted entirely in cassette A  Representative section of the remaining breast in cassette B through F  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LESION TO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
