Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  25 MAY 93 at 16 00 CLINICAL DATA  50 year old female with right mass  status post biopsy which revealed infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  90   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    SEE NOTE  2  BIOPSY SITE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  4  TEN OF TEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF TUMOR  NOTE  The inked resection margins are free of tumor  The residual tumor is present as 2 microscopic foci adjacent to the biopsy cavity  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 34                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   and is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a right breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  The overlying skin ellipse measures 22 x 16 5cm  The nipple is grossly unremarkable  and 1 0cm superior to the nipple is a vertical healed scar measuring 4 0cm  Directly beneath the healed scar is a biopsy cavity which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The biopsy cavity is hemorrhagic and has areas surrounding it which are dark  yellow  and firm  The biopsy cavity is 6 0cm from the deep margin and approximately 1 0cm from the anterior margin  The majority of the breast is remarkable for focal patches of soft  white gray parenchyma which are 3 5cm from the deepest margin  The remainder of the breast is primarly soft  yellow adipose tissue  Section Code  A   nipple B   section of the scar C   superior biopsy cavity D   inferior biopsy cavity E U   medial biopsy cavity F G X   lateral biopsy cavity V W   anterior biopsy cavity H   medial and posterior biopsy cavity I   inferior and posterior biopsy cavity J K L Y Z AA BB   all sections lateral to the biopsy cavity Examination of the axillary contents measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm reveals ten lymph nodes which range in dimension from 0 4cm to 3 0cm  The largest lymph node has focal areas of hemorrhage and fat replacement  Sections of axillary fat and representative lymph nodes are submitted in M   T  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
