  The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 07 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan red fatty lymph node  The fatty tissue is removed and the lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX  1 now as A  The remaining fatty tissue is entirely submitted as B C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of previously blue dyed fibrofatty breast tissue which has a localizing wire in place  There is a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The anterior aspect is black inked  the posterior is blue inked  the superior red inked  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed with thin white fibrous tissue  A discrete lesion is not grossly identified  The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from medial to lateral as follows  D  Medial most margin  E F  Full thickness section  G H  Superior aspect  H is designated area   i  Inferior aspect  J K  Superior aspect  L  Superior aspect  M  Most lateral margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional left breast tissue  is a