 biopsy cavity there is a small firm focus of tan yellow tissue  The surgical resection margins have been inked with India ink  The nipple and areolar are grossly unremarkable  Section Code  A  section of nipple and areolar  B  small ellipse of skin including recent surgical incision  lower outer quadrant   C D  inferior surgical resection margins  representative  E  lateral resection margin  representative  F  superior resection margin  representative   G H  firm yellow nodule  adjacent to biopsy cavity  and closest approximation to the deep inked surgical resection margin  I J K  sections through biopsy cavity and closest approximation to deep inked surgical resection margin  L M  section through biopsy cavity  The remainder of the breast has been sectioned at 1 0cm intervals and reveals unremarkable lobulated adipose tissue and unremarkable breast parenchyma  N  section through unremarkable breast parenchyma  medial breast   The second specimen is labeled  Left breast additional inferior margin  and consists of two fragments of breast tissue  One measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and the other measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimens have not been oriented  Upon sectioning these fragments consists of unremarkable adipose and breast parenchymal tissue  There are no foci of tumor grossly identified  This specimen has been submitted entirely in cassettes O through R  Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY PART B  INFERIOR MARGIN  LEFT BREAST  , Unchecked.
