Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  03 MAY 96 at 16 00 CLINICAL DATA  Forty five year old woman with palpable mass on the left breast  core biopsy revealed undifferentiated carcinoma  Bone scan negative  Presence of axillary adenopathy      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  AMENDED GROSS DESCRIPTION Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 09 MAY 96 at 16 31                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OF FOURTEEN LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is confined to the lymph node  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Edited by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 MAY 96 at 16 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 MAY 96 at 16 21     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh under the patient s name and unit number  are two different specimens  Labeled  left modified radical mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm mastectomy specimen including a REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm unremarkable ellipse of skin  The nipple is also unremarkable  The specimen is inked  Multiple sections through the parenchyma show a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm fairly well defined gray to tan  hard mass located in the lateral aspect  1 3cm from the deep margin  Labeled  left axillary contents is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm fragment of adipose tissue  Fourteen lymph nodes are dissected ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm in largest diameters  Sectioning discloses extensive adipose replacement of the majority of the nodes  One of the nodes shows two white distinctive areas  Section code  J  smaller lymph nodes entirely submitted K M  medium sized lymph nodes  half of each one submitted O  lymph node with white areas P Q  largest lymph node  sectioned  and representative cross section entirely submitted Gross Description by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD          