atory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  accompanied by a radiograph   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 8 x 5 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue with needle localizing wires in place  and a second REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 8cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The large piece is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm tan  ill defined firm mass with multiple foci of tan  gritty material  extending to inked margin  Representative sections of this area is frozen as FX  1  and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is tan white  rubbery with multiple cysts  The mass with surrounding breast tissue are submitted in A through F  Representatives of the remaining tissue are in G through J  The smaller piece consists of predominantly fatty tissue  representative section is submitted in K  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
