ined with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 41     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty piece of breast tissue with a wire and an accompanying mammogram  A discrete mass is palpable centrally  This specimen is inked and sectioned to show a 0 6cm firm and gritty  gray tan mass abutting the margin  Lesion too small to freeze  Submitted in toto in A through D  with lesion in A through B  0 6cm lesion  suspicious for carcinoma  too small to freeze  Await permanents  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   REMOVED_DATE CM LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
