 breast parenchyma between the third and fourth masses contains fibrous  nodular breast parenchyma  A hemorrhagic cavity is present between approximately the  2 o clock  and  3 o clock  positions  It measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  is lined by tan red hemorrhagic lining  and contains tan red pasty material and a metal clip  The cavity extends to 2 5cm from the posterior margin and 4cm from the anterior margin  Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Parenchyma between mass  1   mass  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass  3   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular breast parenchyma adjacent to mass  3   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass  4 to margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Parenchyma between mass  3 and  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire cavity to include posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous breast parenchyma adjacent to the cavity in the outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular breast parenchyma in the central quadrant  Received fresh  labeled  Susan J  Parziale  REMOVED_DATE  left breast mastectomy skin   is a 13 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm linear strip of unremarkable skin  which is inked and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LEFT SENTINEL NODE  1   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   LEFT SENTINEL NODE  2   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 18   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 06 41PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR R