ith this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm fibroadipose tissue fragment which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan  firm  stellate nodule which is too small to freeze  Submitted entirely in A  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in B and C  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  SMALL NODULE GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
