erior margin  greater than 2 5cm from the lateral margin and greater than 7 5cm from the medial margin  Also identified at the lateral aspect of the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area irregular hemorrhagic cavity which may represent previous biopsy site  The cavity extends to within 0 5cm of the posterior  2 0cm of the superior  2 5cm of the anterior  3 5cm of the inferior  2 5cm of the lateral  and 8 5cm of the medial margin  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow adipose tissue with an abundant amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue  in an area where the specimen has been previously inked blue  No other discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   From medial and lateral en face margins  respectively   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the larger nodule to the nearest posterior and superior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of parenchyma between the two described indurated areas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the smaller nodule to the nearest anterior and inferior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the possible biopsy area to the nearest margin  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast anterior margin  stitch marks nipple margin   is a portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  bearing a black suture  denoting the nipple margin  as per the surgeon  The anterior aspect of the specimen  bearing the stitch  is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   is a portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The specimen is palpated and dissected to 