Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 30 CLINICAL DATA  Infiltrating ductal carcinoma of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  1  CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIFOCAL  COMEDO TYPE  MARGINS CLEAR  2  FOCAL ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  3  PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE  SCAR AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION   LEFT  AXILLARY NODES  RESECTION  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH BREAST PRIMARY INVOLVING FIVE OUT OF SIXTEEN  5 16  AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  WITH FOCAL EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 13                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  LUMPECTOMY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   2   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3   SO FEW IN SITU CARCINOMAS HAVE BEEN EVALUATED BY BRDU THAT WE CANNOT PROVIDE A RANGE  MEAN OR MEDIAN TO FACILITATE COMPARATIVE ANALYSIS  Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 93 at 09 10     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative progesterone receptor  Negative Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 AUG 93 at 12 04     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 AUG 93 at 12 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast lumpectomy  is a 9 x 8 x 4cm portion of fibrofatty tissue attached to a skin ellipse which measures 5cm in length and 0 5cm in diameter  Along the skin ellipse is a well healed  longitudinal scar which measures 3 6cm  The specimen margins have been previously cut into but the specimen margins are re approximated and the tissue is inked  Within the center of the specimen  grossly 1 1cm from the nearest surgical margin is a cystic space filled with hemorrhage which measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 3 5cm in greatest dimension  A suture denotes one edge but this is not oriented on the requisition slip  Section Code  A B  biopsy cavity  E G  biopsy cavity with closest surgical margin  H  fibrous tissue near suture  I J  firm  white area near defect on surgical margin measuring approximately 1 1cm in greatest dimensions  K  skin with scar  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab is a portion of fibrofatty tissue which measures 12 x 8 x 3cm in greatest dimensions  Contained within this fibrofatty tissue are multiple lymph nodes  one of which measures 1 5cm in greatest dimensions  This is bisected revealing a soft  gray tumor which is submitted for frozen section diagnosis  1 and a breast work up is done on this tissue  Multiple additional lymph nodes are identified which vary in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm  The largest lymph node appears to be entirely replaced by a white firm to soft tumor  L  section of largest lymph node  M V  remaining lymph nodes  Resident  Julie Fanburg  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE   METASTATIC ANAPLASTIC CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  David L Berger  M D  PART A  LUMPECTOMY PART B  LEFT AXILLARY NODE   report_end  , Unchecked.
