of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 02    REVISED REMOVED_DATE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ill defined  firm area with white streaks  abutting the closest inked surface  corresponding to area of architectural distortion  Area too small to be frozen  Suspicious area submitted in cassette A  the remainder of the specimen in cassettes B through J  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT  SMALL FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA BUT TOO SMALL TO BE FROZEN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
