Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  10 AUG 94 at 19 21 CLINICAL DATA  Fine needle aspirate positive for malignancy  left breast mass and suspicious mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 90   INTRADUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  10   NOTE  The surgical margins are negative for malignancy  No vascular of lymphatic invasion is identified  There is no evidence of malignancy in 10 of 10 axillary lymph nodes  The special stains for estrogen receptors and progesterone receptors will be reported in an addendum  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  17 AUG 94 at 08 22 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     THE CARCINOMA MEASURES REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE GROSS   Added by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  20 AUG 94 at 12 21     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 AUG 94 at 15 07     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm tan skin ellipse with a 3 0cm in diameter inverted tan nipple as well as attached 8 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm tan yellow axillary fatty tail  There is a long stitch at what appears to be the lateral aspect and a short stitch that appears to be at the superior aspect  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm tan  firm  irregular  ill defined mass present  1 8cm from the closest deep margin and 8 0cm from the medial margin  The rest of the breast parenchyma is tan yellow and fatty with irregular  ill defined  fibrotic areas present throughout the specimen  Multiple tan  semifirm  unremarkable lymph nodes  measuring in greatest diameter from 0 2cm to 1 1cm are present in the axillary tail  Representative sections of the mass is frozen as FX 1  SECTION CODE  A  FX 1  representative mass   B  closest soft tissue margin  deep  C F  representative sections of tumor  G  representative nipple  H  representative breast tissue  4 0cm medial to the tumor  I L  lymph nodes  Resident  Horace C  Wu  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST   INVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH AN INTRADUCTAL COMPONENT  MARGINS GROSSLY UNINVOLVED  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  William Thomas Caine  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY    report_end  , Unchecked.
