ates with both the anterior and posterior margins  The cavity lining is hemorrhagic  smooth  and glistening  The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral  and the cavity comes to 0 1cm from the lateral margin  0 7cm from the medial margin  0 5cm from the inferior margin  and 1 0cm from the superior margin and it communicates with the anterior and posterior margins  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow to white and fibrotic  The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from medial to lateral in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the medial margin taken en face in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the lateral radially sectioned in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  report_end  , Checked.
