Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 49 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  MULTIPLE FOCI WITHIN THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Inked margins are free of tumor  no blood or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  The gross diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 35 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 14 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of breast  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm stellate firm white lesion grossly extending to within 0 3cm of the closest inked margin  The lesion is entirely submitted in cassettes A   D  Adjacent normal parenchyma is submitted in cassette E  Please note that 90  of the specimen has been submitted  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
