s with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 27    REVISED REMOVED_DATE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of breast tissue with localizing needle in place and an x ray film  Sectioning reveals a 1 x 1 x 0 6cm slightly firm  comedo type lesion near the needle which approaches to within 0 2cm of the inked margin  A section of the lesion is frozen as FX  1 and submitted in A  The rest of the area corresponding to the calcification is submitted in B through E  The remainder is submitted in F through K  Dr  Ackroyd has retained the radiograph  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  DCIS  HIGH GRADE  COMEDO CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , Checked.
