Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 13 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer in area of 1st bx cavity  DCIS 2nd biopsy cavity  Patient had 2 needle loc biopsy outside hospital  path submitted 4 29 97  today had reexcision of both areas on 1 specimen   2 biopsy cavities                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  AT LEAST 1 0CM AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING MULTIFOCALLY TO THE LATERAL MARGIN   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The size of the invasive carcinoma is difficult to evaluate due to the multifocal type distribution of the invasion  The invasive carcinoma is present associated with the  deep biopsy site  and is also present in tissue located between the two healing biopsy sites  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW TO INTERMEDIATE GRADE  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT AT THE LATERAL MARGIN ASSOCIATED WITH THE DEEP BIOPSY SITE  AND LESS THAN 0 2CM FROM THE LATERAL MARGIN ASSOCIATED WITH THE  SUPERFICIAL BIOPSY SITE  3  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  PRESENT AT THE LATERAL MARGIN  B    NEEDLE LOCALIZING WIRE TAG    GROSS ONLY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 97 at 18 04                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 MAY 97 at 15 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm fibroadipose tissue overlaid by a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm skin ellipse  designated by a long suture for the lateral margin  a short suture for the superior margin and a double stitch suture for the the deep margin  The specimen is inked blue laterally  red   medially  black   superiorly  and yellow   inferiorly  The skin contains a 2 5cm healed surgical scar  The specimen is sectioned to reveal two areas with fat necrosis consistent with previous biopsy sites  The first biopsy site is more superficial and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The fat necrosis extends focally to the superior resection margin  The second biopsy site is deeper in the tissue and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The fat necrosis in the second biopsy site extends focally to the lateral resection margin and 1 7cm to the deep resection margin  The adjacent breast tissue is fibrofatty and focally cystic  Section code  A D  representative sections of the first  superficial  biopsy site with medial  lateral and superior margins A and B  medial  lateral and inferior margin in C and D  E M  the entire second  deep  biopsy site with medial  lateral and superior margins E to I and with medial  lateral and inferior margin in J to M  N O  sections between the two biopsy sites  Also received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  he patient s name  unit number  and  needle localizing wire tag  is a 1 0cm long  0 01cm in diameter metal localizing wire  Gross exam only  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION PART B  BREAST  NEEDLE   BIOPSY   report_end  , Checked.
