                             BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 07 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh for with the patient name  unit number and  right breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm portion of yellow adipose tissue with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the superior margin  The specimen is black  inked and the anterior portion is green inked  Sectioning the specimen reveals REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan white firm stellate lesion which comes to 0 1cm from the anterior and lateral margins and is far away from the other margins  There are two separate small satellite nodules  each approximately 0 5cm  which are located close to the lateral and anterior margins respectively  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Lateral margin C D  and Z  anterior margin  X Y  lateral margin U   representative sections away from biopsy cavity with medial margin  Received fresh  with the patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node  right axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink rubbery lymph node which submitted entirely in toto as E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shave margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in aggregate of yellow breast tissue which is entirely submitted as F H  R T  V  W and AA CC  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of yellow adipose tissue which contains multiple tan red rubbery to tan white firm lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 3cm to 2 5cm in greatest dimension  I  3 whole lymph nodes J  3 whole lymph nodes K  1 bisected lymph node L  1 bisected lymph node M  1 bisected lymph node Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional medial margin right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of yellow adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as N Q  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  WEN JING  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS  PART E  BREAST  ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOP , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 AUG 93 ACCESSIONED ON  16 AUG 93 at 15 21 CLINICAL DATA  Right mammographic abnormality                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2 OF 3  85   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  15    NOTE  The carcinoma measures 0 7cm in greatest dimension  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Intraductal carcinoma is present at the margin  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  18 AUG 93 at 17 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors