Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 11 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  90   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO AND SOLID TYPES  10   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The invasive tumor component comes focally to within 0 1cm of the closest inked resection margin  The tumor measures 1 1cm in largest diameter  There is no unoquivocal vascular invasion noted  The intraductal tumor component is multifocally present away from the invasive tumor portion and comes to within less than 0 1cm of the closest inked resection margin  slide D   Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 20 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 95 at 15 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm yellow red lumpectomy specimen with a localizing wire in place  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm irregular firm  tan to red area suspicious for invasive carcinoma  No frozen section is done because the nodule is too small  The nodule comes to within 0 2cm of the closest inked resection margin grossly  The nodule is submitted in cassettes A and B with the remainder of the specimen in cassettes C  D  and E  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY , Unchecked.
