ly and is exposed at the anterior margin and 4 0cm from the nearest posterior margin  This biopsy cavity is also tan pink to gray white and is lined by granulation tissue  and the wall shows indurated fatty tissue  with foci of hemorrhage and fat necrosis extending up to the anterior margin  Obvious tumor is not identified  The breast parenchyma between the 2 biopsy cavities is mostly fibrotic and firm and shows prominent tan pink glandular tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and pink white fibrous stroma  The subareolar tissue also shows dense fibrosis  Lymph nodes are not identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in the upper outer quadrant  with adjacent breast parenchyma and anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic breast tissue  with prominent glandular tissue  between the 2 cavities  lateral breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in the lower outer quadrant  with surrounding breast parenchyma and nearest anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nearest posterior margin from the biopsy cavity in the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma away from both the biopsy cavities  medial breast   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 22   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 58 27PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Unchecked.
