 of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 97 at 12 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm well circumscribed white to gray  rubbery mass that extends focally to a resection margin  representative sections are frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen to Cox 5  A fragment is taken for possible research  Section Code  A D  representative sections of mass  E H  representative sections of surrounding abnormal tissue  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     Frozen section diagnosis  1  BREAST  EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
