ber  and  final inferior lateral margin  is an unoriented piece of pink tan breast tissue with no stitches  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel node  hot and blue  left axilla  is a specimen consisting of two fragment of breast tissue and lymph node  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  respectively  The larger portion of tissue appears to have a large  focally hemorrhagic lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The lymph node is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The smaller tissue fragment is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  palpable node  left axilla  is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lymph node with attached fatty tissue  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Michael W Lawlor M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael W Lawlor M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART