Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  04 MAY 98 at 13 14 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN AND TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  OCCUPYING 2 OF 6 BLOCKS  AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 98 at 13 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   SPECIMEN  1  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesteron receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 MAY 98 at 16 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  are two small fragments  the larger measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  and the smaller fragment measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The fragments of tissue are inked and serially sectioned to reveal dense white  cystic parenchyma with larger cysts noted in the larger fragment of tissue  The larger fragment is submitted entirely in cassettes A and B with the smaller fragment entirely in cassette C  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm breast fragment with a dense white cystic parenchyma  the largest cyst measuring 0 6cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes D   I  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   BOTH FRAGMENTS NOT SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1 PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  2   report_end  , Checked.
