Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 05 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  80    REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  20    MICROPAPILLARY AND SOLID TYPES WITH NEUROENDOCRINE FEATURES  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  3  ALL  21  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  4  FAT NECROSIS  FIBROSIS AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Definite lymphatic and blood vascular invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 10                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm sheet of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple surgical staples and accompanied with an x ray and a localizing wire within one partially detached fragment at the periphery of the specimen  A 0 8cm nodule is palpable near the localizing wire and a second 0 6cm nodule is palpable in the main part of the specimen  Both nodules are within 0 2cm of the surface of the specimen  The nodule of the periphery of the specimen is white tan on cross section and is submitted in cassettes A and B entirely  Adjacent breast tissue is submitted in cassettes C and D  The central nodule has a red tan cut surface and is consistent with a lymph node and is submitted entirely in cassette E  the remaining breast tissue is sectioned revealing several lymph nodes and is submitted in cassettes F through EE  entirely  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
