ned with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 34     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  Overlying the breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm nipple with a short stitch designating the superior and a long stitch designating the lateral orientation  Sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregular  multinodular  stellate  hard lesion in the superior lateral quadrant  0 7cm from the superior anterior margin and 2 7cm from the deep margin  Although the lesion is multinodular  all of the abnormal areas appear to be contiguous  representing a single lesion  This area of nodular white  fibrous parenchyma extends into the lateral tissue  1 0cm from the anterior margin and 1 7cm from the deep margin  Also present  is a 0 4cm cyst with necrotic brown material in the center  The cyst is 0 6cm from the closest margin which is the superior anterior margin  SECTION CODE  A B  stellate lesion with closest superior anterior margin  C  cyst with necrotic material and superior anterior margin  D  firm tissue in lateral breast with closest anterior margin  E  firm tissue posterior to nipple  F  closest deep margin to stellate lesion  Dissected from the axillary fat  are multiple lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest diameter  Sections of the nodes are submitted in G through I  The largest node is submitted alone in I  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  G  Gregory Gallico III  M D  Steven Joseph Nisco  M D  PART   BREAST AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
