anging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension are identified in the axillary portion of the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in its relationship to the deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in its relationship to the anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in its relationship to the skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section of the biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary lymph node  Gross Dictation by Julia Turbiner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  None provided  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  2  FOCAL LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE x 6 0 cm right mastectomy specimen  with a REMOVED_DATE x 12 5 cm tan skin ellipse  There is a suture designating the axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2 cm unremarkable nipple areolar complex and a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5 cm defect within the skin at the 7 o clock position  5 0cm from the nipple  This defect communicates with an underlying biopsy cavity  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5 cm biopsy cavity  communicating with the previously described skin defect  The biopsy cavity is within the lower inner quadrant and is 1 5cm from the closest anterior soft tissue margin and 2 0cm from the closest posterior margin  The biopsy cavity is lined by red to white fibrous tissue and is surrounded by focal areas of chalky yellow adipose tissue with no discrete masses or lesions identified  Two surgical clips are identified within the lining of the biopsy cavity  An additional surgical clip is ident