Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 58 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE II III EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  SINGLE FOCUS OF LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  NOTE  The tumor is 3 5cm in greatest dimension  Lymphatic invasion is present  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 40                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  EXCISION   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   9   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    The assay is suboptimal due to background staining  If the information will be used for clinical decisions  confirmation with flow cytometry is advised  Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 93 at 09 05     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 141 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive 968 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 AUG 93 at 12 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  and is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty tissue fragment  which is unoriented  containing a palpable  very firm mass  The specimen is inked and sectioned to show a tan gray mass occupying most of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  This mass extends to several inked resection margins  and has an irregular border and gritty sensation on sectioning  A representative portion of this mass is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue is sent for estrogen receptors and BRDU  Representative sections showing where the tumor approaches the inked margin are submitted as A through F   The tumor submitted as A and B appears to grossly abut the inked resection margin   Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Lisa H  Lerner  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 24 CLINICAL DATA  76 year old female status post REMOVED_DATE abnormal mammogram with Grade II infiltrating carcinoma by biopsy  margins extensively involved   Now presents for follow up lumpectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST MASS  LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  ONE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  SLIDE E   2  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  SLIDE F   3  SURGICAL EXCISION SITE  WITH MULTINUCLEATED HISTIOCYTES  BREAST  SUPERIOR   BIOPSY  UNREMARKABLE CAUTERIZED BREAST  BREAST  INFERIOR   BIOPSY  UNREMARKABLE BREAST  BREAST  MEDIAL   BIOPSY  CAUTERIZED BREAST WITH ONE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  BREAST  RIGHT LATERAL   BIOPSY  UNREMARKABLE BREAST  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 52 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five parts  Labeled  Re excision breast cancer  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm  tan pink and yellow  soft tissue mass with a 4 x 0 7cm skin ellipse running longitudinally  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a mottled tan and yellow cut surface  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm hemorrhagic cyst near one pole of the specimen  Representative sections through the specimen are submitted in cassettes A through F  with cyst containing sections in cassettes A through C  Labeled  Superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  yellow white  soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette G  Labeled  Inferior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  yellow  soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette H  Labeled  Medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  tan  soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette I  Labeled  Lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan and brown  soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette J  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  RIGHT  PART B  LATTERAL  BIOPSY  RIGHT  PART C  INFERIOR  BIOPSY  RIGHT  PART D  MEDIAL  BIOPSY  RIGHT  PART E  LATERAL  BIOPSY  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
