rough K  The smaller fragment is serially sectioned to reveal a pink white with focal red cut surface and is entirely submitted in L and M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  short inferior  long lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm irregularly shaped  yellow blue  firm breast with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm skin ellipse remarkable for a central linear scar  A REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm defect is present on the posterior aspect of the specimen  The superior half of the specimen above this defect is inked in blue and the inferior aspect of the specimen below the defect is inked in black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 4cm biopsy cavity with hemorrhagic wall which grossly abuts the posterior margin and extends to 0 1cm from the anterior margin  0 4cm from the superior  inferior and lateral margins and 0 8cm from the medial margin  SECTION CODE  N  representative section of biopsy cavity with closest posterior margin from the medial aspect of specimen  O  representative section of biopsy cavity with anterior margin from lateral aspect of specimen  P  Superior margin of the biopsy cavity 0 8cm from the lateral margin  Q  Inferior margin and biopsy cavity 0 8cm from the lateral most margin  R  Representative section of the biopsy cavity with the anterior surface overinked in red  Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL    EX