Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  01 AUG 97 at 11 28 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  SEE NOTE   CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH FEATURES OF BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  Extra nodal soft tissue extension of carcinoma is present in 1 lymph node  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 15 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a modified radical mastectomy with an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with an unremarkable nipple  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm hard  tan white mass that extends to 0 5cm from the nearest margin  Representative sections from the tumor are included in A D  The specimen including the nearest margin is in D  Two representative sections from the tissue away from the tumor is included in cassette E F  Axillary nodes are dissected and submitted in G N  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
