Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  24 MAY 94 at 14 28 CLINICAL DATA  Mass by mammogram and palpation                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE   95    REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO WITHIN LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED MARGIN  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBIFORM TYPE   5     SEE NOTE   NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  The results on estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 94 at 14 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 6cm in greatest dimension  ill defined  tan white  gritty and firm area that grossly abuts an inked resection margin  The remainder of the specimen is predominantly composed of unremarkable breast and adipose tissue  A representative section of the lesion is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Representative sections of remainder of the specimen submitted in cassettes A through J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
