Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  05 AUG 97 at 10 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  PHYLLODES TUMOR  29 0 CM   LOW GRADE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor displays  2 mitotic figures per 10 HPF  and lacks marked cellular pleomorphism  Stromal overgrowth is not seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed this case and agrees with the diagnosis  2  ALL  12  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF TUMOR    LYMPH NODES   RIGHT AXILLA   ALL  5  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  1   SKIN WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  2   SKIN WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 18 06                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  are four parts  Labeled with patient s name only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 14 0cm mastectomy specimen with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 27 0cm ellipse of skin with an eccentrically placed 5 0cm nipple aveolar complex and a 14  x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  On external examination  a large multi nodular  tumor occupies the majority   95   of the specimen  the tumor does not grossly involve the deep margin  Cross sectioning of the mastectomy specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm  multi lobulated  well defined mass which compresses the normal surrounding breast tissue  The cut surface reveals numerous white whorled bulging  firm  rubbery lobulations  The lobulations range in diameter from 10 0cm to less than 0 2cm  In between the lobulations are cyst like and slit like spaces  the largest of which is 4 0cm in greatest length  and 0 3cm in width  The interface of the tumor with the surrounding breast parenchyma is grossly non infiltrative  No areas of hermorrhage or necrosis are seen  A representative section of the specimen is frozen as FX 1  and submitted as A  a section of the closest deep resection margin is submitted in B C  Representative sections from different areas of the tumor mass are submitted in D U  Sections taken from the cyst like area are submitted in H I  Representative sections of tumor interfacing with surrounding breast parenchyma in S T  A section containing a small comedo like area submitted in U  The surrounding breast parenchyma is sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  No additional masses are found  Representative sections of unremarkable breast parenchyma are submitted in V W  Section of the axillary tail reveals multiple  red  firm lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 2cm  All lymph nodes are submitted in W through BB  Received in a separate container   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name only is an REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm skin ellipse with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm adipose tissue  The surface of the skin ellipse and cut surface of the adipose tissue are unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in CC  Received in a separate container  labeled  lymph nodes  are three fragments of adipose tissue which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in total aggregate  The adipose tissue is dissected to reveal multiple  tan  firm lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 3cm to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  All submitted in DD through EE  Received in a separate container   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number is an REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  unremarkable skin ellipse with attached underlying adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm in greatest dimension  A representative section of skin is submitted in FF  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  FAVOR PHYLLOIDES TUMOR  O R  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST AND SKIN TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 12 CLINICAL DATA  Excision breast lesion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  98   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  2   CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The focus of infiltrating carcinoma measures 0 7cm on the slide  The surgical resection margins are free of tumor  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying x ray of the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 8cm ill defined  soft  red tan area extending to within 0 2cm of the inked margin  adjacent to the thick end of wire  The remaining parenchyma is composed of soft  lobulated  unremarkable adipose tissue  The nodule is submitted in A F  The adjacent parenchyma and firmer areas from the remaining parenchyma are submitted in G O  Resident  Asif Rashid  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT EXCISION  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION THAT IS LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  George S Richardson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST LESION   report_end  , Unchecked.
