E x 5 0cm left simple mastectomy with a stitch designating the axillary end  The anterior is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan skin ellipse contains a 3 0cm nipple areola complex  A REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm curvilinear scar is present along the REMOVED_DATE o clock edge of the areola complex  The remainder of the skin surface is grossly unremarkable  Underlying the scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm biopsy cavity filled with a tan brown hemorrhagic material and lined by a granular tan tissue with a surrounding punctate yellow areas  The biopsy cavity comes to within 1 5cm of the nearest deep margin  5 0cm from the superior edge  and 0 8cm from the skin surface  At the lateral edge of the cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic nodular area coming to within 2 0cm of the nearest deep margin  In addition  a 1 0cm in diameter clear fluid filled cyst is identified 1 5cm inferior to the biopsy cavity  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  No lymph nodes are identified within the axillary tail  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of biopsy cavity  cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  biopsy cavity to posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic nodular area  1 4cm     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of 1 0cm clear fluid filled parenchymal cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of breast parenchyma  medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of breast parenchyma  lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of axillary tail  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  LYMPH NODE    SENTINEL  PRIMARY 321   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE   SENTINEL  SECONDARY 53   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  3  LYMPH NODE   SENTINEL   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Chad Soupir M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Chad Soupir M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  PRIMARY  SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SECONDARY  SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART E  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 MAY 04 ACCESSIONED ON  21 MAY 04 at 15 51 CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma on prior FNA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Grade  2  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested on block A  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   MASTECTOMY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 04 at 11 44                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 04 at 16 13 Proofread by  Carole Fleming  Autopsy Secretary     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block A   HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER 2 neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  28 MAY 04 at 12 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen which includes an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm tan white ellipse of skin  There is a central inverted nipple  No scars identified on the skin surface  The deep margin has several fragments of attached soft  tan red muscle measuring up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  The anterior margin is marked with blue ink  and the posterior margin is marked with black inked  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  tan tumor with irregular borders which extends to 1 3cm of the deep margin and is located adjacent to the nipple on the skin surface  There are no other masses or nodules are grossly identified  The tissue consist predominantly of adipose tissue with approximately 40 percent of the specimen consisting of soft  white fibrous tissue  The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Multiple lymph nodes are located in the fat which measures up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm which have soft tan cut surfaces  Representative sections are submitted as  A D  Tumor from inferior medial to superior lateral aspect  E F  Sections away from tumor  G  Nipple  H  One intact node  proximal REMOVED_DATE of axilla  I  One bisected node  proximal REMOVED_DATE J  One bisected lymph node proximal REMOVED_DATE K  One intact lymph node  mid portion of axilla  L  One bisected lymph node  mid portion of axilla  M N  One lymph node in five parts  mid portion of axilla  O  Four intact lymph nodes  distal REMOVED_DATE of axilla  P  One bisected lymph node  distal REMOVED_DATE of axilla  Q  One lymph node trisected  distal portion of axilla  Gross Description by  TIM J  ROBINSON Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  John Dekker  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Revised Report            Reason for Amendment  1  Corrected Transcription Error not in Final Diagnosis CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 52 year old woman with a recent diagnosis of invasive breast cancer who has undergone neoadjuvant chemotherapy  She now presents for a right breast lumpectomy  short superior  long lateral  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  See table 1 and note  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  Microscopic foci  See note  GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to   0 1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within  and beyond  the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ is positive at the superior  anterior and lateral margins of the specimen along broad fronts  NOTE  The tumor is present as multiple small microscopic nests and trabeculae as well as single tumor cells in a background of dense sclerosis  This finding likely reflects prior chemotherapy with near complete resolution of the tumor mass  Immunohistochemical stains for p63  myosin  calponin and cytokeratin were performed on sections  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Although limited by sectioning artifact  the immunohistochemical stains support the diagnosis of residual invasive ductal carcinoma  The DCIS is present on at least 8 of 10 sections of the breast  The diagnosis of DCIS is complicated by the affect of prior neoadjuvant chemotherapy which accentuates the cytologic atypia in the areas of DCIS  Notably a field defect with changes in benign ductal cells is not observed  We considered the possibility that the cytologic changes are purely artifactual and secondary to the chemotherapy  rather than representing residual DCIS  However  the degree of cytological atypia in the involved ducts as well as the extent of the changes and the presence of architectural abnormalities strongly favors a diagnosis of DCIS  An immunohistochemical stain for keratin REMOVED_DATE performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  shows focal staining in luminal ductal cells  however  we interpret this finding as nonspecific in the setting of neoadjuvant chemotherapy  Overall  the findings are interpreted as residual invasive and in situ ductal carcinoma in the setting of prior neoadjuvant chemotherapy  Dr  Melinda Lerwill has reviewed this case and concurs with the diagnosis  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   is a lumpectomy specimen oriented by 2 sutures measuring 4 8cm x 3 6cm x 1 1cm  The specimen is inked anterior black  posterior   blue  medial  green  lateral   yellow  A needle localization wire is present and an x ray is provided demonstrating the positions of 2 metal clips relative to the wire  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal tan white nodular breast tissue with areas of hemorrhage  The helical clip is identified in one section and adjacent to this clip is a tan firm mass embedded in white fibrous tissue  The mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and is located 0 5cm from the closest anterior margin  0 5cm from the closest medial margin  1 4cm from the closest posterior margin  1 6cm from the closest lateral margin  1 6cm from the closest superior margin  2 0cm from the closest inferior margin  The second S shaped clip is not identified  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First superior section taken after en face margin  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Next section  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Next section containing white fibrous areas divided into 3 pieces   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor with closest black inked anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor with closest green medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of uninvolved breast  Amended report  1  Corrected transcription error not in final diagnosis  This report has been revised to correct a transcription error in Table  1  The prior report had the statement  cannot evaluate  under the headings of invasive and in situ carcinoma  We have deleted these statements and specified the margins for DCIS  The prior report should be disregarded  Dr  Michele Specht was notified of the changes on REMOVED_DATE at 9 30 am  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  1 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Right   Excision  report_end  , Checked.
