el node  2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm soft tan tissue which is entirely frozen as FX  2 and resubmitted as B  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a lumpectomy specimen measuring 9 x 7 x 5cm with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm wrinkled  tan skin ellipse containing a 3 5cm well healed  linear scar  There is a short stitch designating the superior margin  and a long stitch designating the lateral margin  The specimen is inked black and the anterior margin is overinked blue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity  0 5cm to the closest margin  inferior   The cavity contains a shaggy  induration inner lining  No papillary excrescences are identified  Further sectioning of the cavity reveals it to be directly subjacent to the skin with a possible connection to the anterior superior margin  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow and lobular  Representative sections are submitted as follows  C  Cavity to include margins  D E  Cavity to include superior anterior margin  F G  Cavity  H  Representative parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional breast tissue  is an 8 x 3 x 0 5cm oblong portion of tan yellow  lobular fat with a stitch on one side denoting  new margin  which is inked black  The specimen is cross sectioned and representative sections are submitted in I through L  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral margin  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan yellow  lobular fragment of fat with a stitch on one side denoting the new margin which is inked black  The specimen is sectioned and representative sections are submitted in cassettes M through P  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  new inferior margin right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm tan yellow  lob