Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 05 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  Note  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  RARE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of yellow fibrofatty tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal hard  white  stellate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm mass  approaching to within less than 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  Specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes A through J  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST  LEFT   GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  NOT LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Robert Gerdes Ojemann  M D  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
