ph nodes are identified in the axillary tail attached to the mass  These lymph nodes range in size from REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Section Code  A C  Representative sections of largest biopsy cavity and adjacent anterior margin  D E  Small nodule between two biopsy cavities and small biopsy cavity along with adjacent anterior margin  F  Small biopsy cavity with adjacent anterior margin  G  Region between two biopsy cavities  H I  Representative sections of second nodule  away from biopsy cavities  J  Representative section of closest  posterior  margin to the second nodule  K L  Representative sections of fibrous areas away from biopsy cavities and nodules  located in the medial portion of the specimen  M O  Largest lymph node  trisected  submitted entirely  P Q  Second largest lymph node  bivalved  submitted entirely  R S  Large lymph nodes  bivalved  submitted entirely in separate cassettes  T U  More axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  upper inner quadrant  superficial tissue  left breast   are two fragments of fibrofatty tissue measuring 5 x 3 x 1 and 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  These specimens are inked and serially sectioned to reveal no focal abnormalities  Representative sections of the two fragments of tissue are submitted as cassette V  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional left axillary tissue   are multiple fragments of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue measuring 7 x 3 x 3cm in aggregate  The tissue is dissected to reveal two lymph nodes  one measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  the other measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  A radial section of the largest node and the entire smaller node are submitted in cassettes W  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional superficial tissue  upper outer quadrant  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 2 5cm fibrofatty fragment of tissue  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal no focal abnormalities  just unremarkable breast tissue  A representative section is submitted as cassette X  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  upper quadrant superficial mass   are multiple fragments of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue measuring 6 x 4 x 1 5cm in aggregate  The tissue is entirely submitted as cassettes Y HH  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  GRAY OR 34 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST SUPERFICIAL TISSUE  UPPER INNER QUADRANT  PART C  AXILLARY TISSUE ADDITIONAL LEFT  PART D  BREAST SUPERFICIAL TISSUE  UPPER OUTER QUADRANT  PART E  BREAST SUPERFICIAL TO MASS  UPPER QUADRANT  , Unchecked.
