Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 26 CLINICAL DATA  Eleven year history of left breast cancer  Treated with lumpectomy  radiation and chemotherapy  Now with right breast nipple retraction  Needle biopsy shows adenocarcinoma  Bone scan on REMOVED_MONTH 20th                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY AND  RIGHT ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH FOCAL APOCRINE FEATURES  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III III   WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Blood vascular invasion is not seen  Resection margins are free of carcinoma  Ductal carcinoma in situ is associated with the invasive tumor suggesting primary origin in the right breast  However  the carcinoma has similar histology to the previous left carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and thus a metastasis can not be completely excluded  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  INTERMEDIATE GRADE   ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE CARCINOMA  3  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 4 OF 15 LYMPH NODES WITH EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 56                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a mastectomy specimen REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm and 900 grams  designated with a short stitch for superior aspect and a long stitch for lateral aspect  with a REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm skin ellipse containing a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm retracted nipple  A 5 5cm well healed surgical scar is present 1 5cm superior to the nipple  Attached to the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan to pink focally yellow firm mass under the nipple and 1 8cm from the closest  deep  inked resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is mostly fatty with some fibrous area medial to the main mass  SECTION CODE  A E  representative sections of tumor F  nipple with underlying tumor G  nearest deep resection margin  radial section H  fibrous area with nearest deep resection margin I J  and K  axillary lymph nodes  Also received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm adipose tissue  submitted entirely in cassettes L  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURG   ACC 457 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
