led REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Left breast mass  is a 9 x 8 x 3cm fragment of breast tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm unremarkable skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 4cm in diameter hard  irregular  tan gray nodule which is 0 5cm from the closest deep margin and 0 2cm deep to the overlying skin in the center of the specimen  Representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Section Code  A  no A  B  tumor showing deepest extension  C  tumor  D  section of tumor showing relationship to overlying skin  E  unremarkable skin  Resident  Jason Lockridge  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Andrea Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   LEFT INFLAMMATORY FOLD MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 16 CLINICAL DATA  41 y o  female with right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  THREE NODULES  6 8  REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  WITH DIRECT EXTENSION INTO THE DERMIS AND EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  INCLUDING EXTENSIVE DERMAL LYMPHATIC INVASION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is present adjacent to and extends away from the biopsy cavity  The skeletal muscle is not directly involved by tumor  although foci of lymphatic invasion are present within the muscle  Stromally invasive tumor is  0 2cm from the margins  however  tumor present within lymphatic vessels is focally present  0 1cm from the deep margin  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 52                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  skin  areola  nipple  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm right simple mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 11 5cm tan skin ellipse  There is a central REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm brown areola with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple  There is a 5 0cm linear scar  which is 2 8cm superomedial to the nipple and comes to 1 4cm of the margin  The margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of attached tan red muscle along the deep aspect and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm gray pink fibrous cavity consistent with previous biopsy site  which abuts the muscle and comes to 0 5cm of the deep margin  Along the inferolateral aspect of the cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm indurated gray white focally hemorrhagic tumor mass  which comes to 1 4cm of the deep margin  Also noted is a discontinuous REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated gray pink nodule  which abuts the interior aspect of the cavity and comes to 1 5cm of the deep margin  There is a third REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm indurated gray white focally hemorrhagic tumor mass along the superior aspect of the cavity which comes to 1 5cm of the deep and superficial margins  The remaining cut surface is 7  tan yellow adipose and 30  gray white fibrous tissue  and sectioning of the axillary region reveals possible lymph nodes Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODES  A B  tumor to deep margin  C   tumor to deep margin and cavity  D   tumor to cavity  E   second inferior tumor nodule to cavity and deep margin  F   third superior tumor mass to cavity and deep margin  G   third tumor mass to superficial margin  H   tumor to nipple  I   away from tumor  J K  possible lymph nodes  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  MJF                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 MAY 95 at 16 05 CLINICAL DATA  46 year old female with right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 7 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT A FRACTION OF A MM FROM AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  MICROCYSTS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No ductal carcinoma in situ is identified  AXILLA  RIGHT   RESECTION  CARCINOMA METASTATIC TO 3 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  3 16   Diagnosis by  Jeoffry Brennick  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 47 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS  BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate specimens   Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm unoriented breast excision specimen  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan  firm  somewhat well defined mass  extending to less than 1mm from an inked resection margin  Representative sections in A D  Next to the periphery of the lesion is a tan  soft  ill defined area which extends to the inked margin  representative section in E   Right axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary lymph node dissection containing multiple nodules  REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest diameter  representative sections in F J  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLA  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
