Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Elena F Brachtel  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mastectomy  stitch 12 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH EXTENSIVE NECROSIS  RECENT HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SKIN WITH SCAR AND STROMAL FIBROSIS WITH COARSE CALCIFICATIONS  CONSISTENT WITH PREVIOUS SURGICAL PROCEDURE  SEE TABLE  SEE NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  gross measurement   GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma is located adjacent to the fibrous scar and infiltrates into the lower dermis  There is a marked inflammatory reaction between tumor and skin  no invasion of dermal lymphatic vessels is seen  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a 26 x 21 x 4cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 12 o clock  The anterior surface contains a 25 x 14cm tan brown skin ellipse which bears a 4 x 4cm areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nipple which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 1 x 1 x 0 4cm tan red nodule located approximately between 9 and 10 o clock on the overlying tan brown skin  6 5cm from the areola  The skin around this nodule is erythematous and indurated  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a stellate scar  a necrotic mass and a calcified nodule  The tan white stellate fibrotic scar in the outer quadrant  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  lies approximately between 9 and 10 o clock position   0 1cm from the posterior inked margin and 0 3cm from overlying skin  Adjacent and abutting the stellate scar there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm tan yellow ill defined  necrotic mass which grossly abuts the nodule on the overlying skin and lies 2 5cm from posterior inked margin  Approximately 0 8cm medial to the scar in the lower quadrant  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan white fairly well circumscribed calcified nodule which lies 4cm from the posterior inked margin and 3 5cm from overlying skin  The breast parenchyma between the 2 nodules is dense white  rubbery and fibrous  The remaining breast parenchyma contains diffusely tan white rubbery nodular fibrous tissue interspersed with a moderate amount of tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No additional discrete masses or lesions are noted  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are gross appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic scar to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic scar to include adjacent necrotic mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Necrotic mass to overlying skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Calcified nodule to include closest posterior inked margin submitted following decalcification   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma  between the necrotic mass and the calcified nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma  central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous breast parenchyma  inner quadrant  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 21 02PM ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 35 36PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 MAY 99 ACCESSIONED ON  07 MAY 99 at 15 40 CLINICAL DATA  None given                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     COLON  FOCAL ILEAL ISCHEMIA WITH TRANSMURAL NECROSIS  PERFORATION  AND EXTRAMURAL ABSCESS FORMATION ASSOCIATED WITH MESENTERIC ARTERIAL THROMBOSIS AND COMPLETE OCCLUSION  SLIDE D   MARGINS OF RESECTION ARE HISTOLOGICALLY VIABLE  BREAST  LEFT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   SEVERAL MICROSCOPIC FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Residual invasive carcinoma is not seen  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins are free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 99 at 10 49 Consulting Pathologist s   Carolyn C  Compton  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  L Breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 10 8cm ellipse of tan nipple bearing skin  On the skin  there is a 3 8cm curvilinear  healing scar that runs along the superior aspect of the nipple  which is inverted  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm healing biopsy cavity with a tan pink lining membrane  The cavity comes to 1 8cm from the posterior margin and 1 8cm from the anteroinferior margin  and grossly abuts the skin  The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity are submitted from medial to lateral in Cassettes H K  with the inverted nipple in Cassette I  The closest posterior margin is submitted in Cassette L  the closest anteroinferior margin is submitted in Cassette M  and representative sections of unremarkable parenchyma are also in Cassettes L M  as well as N O  No lymph nodes are found in the axillary portion of the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Ileal Colon   is an 8 0cm portion of cecum and a 45 0cm portion of attached ileum  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm transmural defect  located at 7 0cm from the ileocecal junction and the surrounding mesentery necrosis and fibrinous adhesions  Opening the specimen reveals that the perforation site has a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm area showing mucosal necrosis with yellow brown discoloration and sharp demarcation from adjacent dark red mucosa  The entire ileal colon specimen is examined to find no definite tumor lesion on the mucosal surface  Sectioning of the mesentery revealed nodular  appearing adhesions and fat necrosis  Also received in the same container is a 10 0cm unoriented portion of small intestine with a side to side anastomosis to a 7 0cm portion of the small intestine  The anastomosis site has a fresh suture  and the mucosa of both small intestine fragments are dark red with edema  SECTION CODE  A   Proximal ileal resection margin  B   Distal colonic resection margin  C   Representative section from the perforation site  D   Representative section from the mesentery  E   Anastomosis site  F G  End from the anastomosis  Gross Description by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  COLON PART B  BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
