ormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  breast left  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a suture at one end marking the lateral margin  The entire specimen is inked and black  and the lateral margin is overinked in blue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined  white tan firm area with hemorrhage abutting several margins  including the lateral margin  The lesion relative to closest margins is entirely submitted in A D  Representative sections of parenchyma distal to the lesion are submitted in cassettes E F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm fragment of red tan fatty soft tissue with multiple surgical clips  Lymph nodes from the specimen are submitted in G I  G representing one lymph node   Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  ILL DEFINED  FOCALLY FIRM AREA  GROSSLY AT INKED MARGIN HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Lawrence T Geoghegan  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION   report_end  , Unchecked.
