men  0 3cm from the deep margin and 5 0cm from the medial margin grossly  The remaining breast shows predominantly fibrous tissue with cystic areas in the majority of the specimen and yellow adipose tissue in the inferior portion and axillary tail  Representative sections submitted  Section code  C D  biopsy site with closest  anterior  margin E  biopsy site F H  deep margin overlying biopsy site I K  medial firm area with deep margin L M  nodular medial breast tissue   fibrocystic change N  medial cystic areas O  representative superior margin  3cm from biopsy site  P R  Additional tissue  adjacent to biopsy site and superior medial portion of specimen  includes anterior margin  R S  Additional biopsy site T  nipple and areola U  representative superior lateral V  representative inferior lateral W  representative inferior X  axillary tail  This region is sectioned extensively for lymph nodes and none are found   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast medial  is a triangular portion of tan pink skin  REMOVED_DATE x 3 1cm with underlying soft tissue  REMOVED_DATE x 7 x 2cm in greatest dimension  The cut sections show greater than 90  unremarkable yellow adipose tissue admixed with scant  white fibrous tissue with no grossly suspicious areas  Representative sections  including all fibroglandular tissue  are submitted in cassettes EE through II  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lateral  is a roughly triangular portion of unremarkable tan pink skin  9 x 3 1cm in greatest dimensions with underlying soft tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 7cm in greatest dimensions  Multiple cross sections through the specimen show a solid area of white  fibrous tissue  approximately REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1cm in greatest dimension  A representative section submitted in cassettes JJ through QQ  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  un