ession  weak to moderate complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells     Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not  been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The  FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this  laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision            Electronically Signed Out By  Atul K Bhan MBBS  MD on REMOVED_DATE 15 08       CLINICAL HISTORY  Breast cancer     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST MASTECTOMY  LEFT  B  LYMPH NODES DISSECTION  LEFT AXILLA    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     A  Received fresh  labeled  left mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the 12 o clock and a long  suture designating lateral  The REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm overlying skin is unremarkable   The nipple and areola appear unremarkable  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin inked black  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm gray white  fibrotic scar in the central  subareolar breast that is 0 5cm  from the posterior margin  extends to the skin surface  and is 0 6cm of the  anterior margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated  tan pink area at the  periphery of the scar that is 0 5cm from the posterior margin  A metallic clip  is seen within the scar  The surrounding tissue consists of yellow white   fibrofatty tissue  Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral breast  The  following representative sections are submitted      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire firm area at the edge of the scar  including posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional 