Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 54 CLINICAL DATA  History of lobular carcinoma with negative lymph nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma focally abuts an inked resection margin  the in situ component extends to within 1 0mm of an inked margin  No definite lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Tumor is present throughout the entire specimen  measuring 4 0cm on gross examination  Receptor studies will be done on the formalin fixed tissue  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue with a central firmness to palpation  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 3cm firm white area within less than 0 3cm of an inked surface  The remainder of the tissue is unremarkable  The lesion is submitted in cassettes A and B  the remainder of the tissue is in C through G  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     Gross Dx  RIGHT BREAST MASS   EXCISION  SMALL LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
