Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 37 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a 2 8x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of breast  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm firm  well circumscribed nodule abutting the inked margin  The nodule is submitted in casettes A and B  The remainders are submitted entirely in cassettes C and D  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS NODULE TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 AUG 98 at 14 03 CLINICAL DATA  Breast carcinoma  Pre operative chemotherapy for bilateral breast cancer  Clinically positive right axillary nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  Note  The tumor dimensions are difficult to ascertain due to treatment effects  While the greatest dimension of any single focus of invasive carcinoma is 1 5cm  foci of carcinoma are present in multiple slides from an area grossly measuring 4cm in greatest dimension  Focal perineural invasion is seen  No angiolymphatic invasion is identified  The deep margin of resection is negative  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL   BIOPSY  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  CONFINED TO THE LYMPH NODE  Note  Metastatic carcinoma is not present in the tissue sampled for frozen section evaluation  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  AT LEAST 3 CM  WITH FOCAL MUCINOUS PATTERN  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  Note  The grade of the invasive carcinoma is difficult to assess due to treatment effect  but is estimated to be grade 2  Focal perineural invasion is present  No angiolymphatic invasion is seen  The deep margin of resection is negative  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  06 AUG 98 at 18 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen recpetor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 13 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is inked and bisected to reveal a brown focally yellow cut surface  One fourth is frozen as FX 1  which is resubmitted in cassette A  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes B   C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left simple mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left mastectomy specimen partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm grossly unremarkable ellipse of skin centered by a grossly unremarkable 1 0cm nipple  