Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 50 CLINICAL DATA  58 y o  with mammographic abnormality and core biopsy positive for cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III   EXTENDING REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is not seen  Definite DCIS is not seen  The tumor displays some  but not all  of the features of medullary carcinoma  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  21  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of breast tissue with a localizing wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fairly well circumscribed tan pink fleshy nodule coming to within 0 1cm of the inked surface  adjacent to the nodule is a more ill defined firm fibrous tissue  The nodule and surrounding tissue is submitted in cassettes A E  A representative section of the breast away from the nodule in cassette F  The remainder of the breast is grossly unremarkable  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  new reexcision superior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of breast tissue with true superior margin inked in blue  The tissue is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes G J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  A representative section from each lymph node is submitted in cassettes L R  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   DISCRETE NODULE WITH SURROUNDING FIRM    INFILTRATIVE LESION  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  2   REEXCISION SUPERIOR MARGIN   NO DISCRETE LESION IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  Janey Sue Pratt  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION , Unchecked.
