Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 27 CLINICAL DATA  56 year old female with left breast calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  90    AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM  SOLID  AND COMEDO TYPES  10    SEE NOTE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 5cm in greatest dimension on histologic section  The inked resection margin is positive for carcinoma  A single focus of lymphatic invasion is seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm mass of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire and accompanying x ray  This specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan firm nodule with irregular borders containing a central 0 1cm hemorrhagic cavity  This nodule extends to the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of this specimen is submitted entirely in A through J  with the nodule in C through E  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
