Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 MAY 03 ACCESSIONED ON  09 MAY 03 at 12 07 CLINICAL DATA  Stitch   12 00  Right simple mastectomy for known breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FIBROADENOMAS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NO RESIDUAL IN SITU OR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  13 MAY 03 at 18 38                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 1 540 gram  31 x 17 x 6cm mastectomy specimen which is oriented by the surgeon with a stitch designating  12 o clock   The overlying 28 x 13cm tan skin has a well healed 7 0cm linear scar  3 8cm right of the nipple  The REMOVED_DATE x 5 3cm nipple areolar complex has an inverted nipple  Adjacent to the scar  within the parenchyma  is a 6 x 7 x 4cm cavity with a tan red  hemorrhagic  ragged lining  The cavity is 0 8cm from the deep margin  The remaining parenchyma is fibrofatty  The fibrous tissue is dense and coarsely granular  5cm medial to the biopsy cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm well circumscribed  firm  rubbery  tan white nodule which is 1 0cm from the nearest margin  Towards the lateral aspect is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm  tan white nodule  questioning intra parenchymal lymph node  Within the lateral superior aspect  5cm from the biopsy cavity  a 7 x 4cm area of the deep margin is tan red  hemorrhagic and membraneous with underlying fibrosis and fat necrosis  No lymph nodes are identified within the lateral tissues  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code  A C  Cavity to deep margin  D  Cavity  E F  Mass medial to cavity  G  Deep margin  closest to mass  H  Parenchyma away from cavity and mass  I  Parenchyma away from cavity and mass to deep margin  J  Hemorrhagic  membraneous area of deep margin  K    intra parenchymal lymph node  Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  DAVID COON  PhD  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
