_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Note  Although the two large nodules of carcinoma have similar morphologic features  they are clearly separate from one another grossly and have associated ductal carcinoma in situ  favoring that they are two separate primary tumors  The smaller foci of invasive carcinoma are also associated with ductal carcinoma in situ and with lymphatic invasion  in one focus   Therefore these too may represent independent primaries  or  in the case of the one focus associated with lymphatic invasion  may have arisen from intra mammary spread of tumor  Immunohistochemical stains for p63  calponin and heavy chain myosin support the absence of myoepithelial cells in one of the small foci of invasive carcinoma  slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Stains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and Factor VIII antigen confirm the presence of lymphatic invasion  The tumor cells contain abundant clear to eosinophilic granular cytoplasm  however PAS stain with and without diastase digestion are negative for the presence of glycogen SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OUT OF ONE LYMPH NODE   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lymph node  which is bisected  and submitted in its entirety as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm yellow pink simple mastectomy  with a central 3 7cm circular white skin ellipse  There is a stitch designating 12 o clock  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm everted nipple  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal two tan white firm irregular lesions measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The smaller lesion is central and comes to within 1 3cm of the deep margin and 1 7cm of the anterior margin  The larger lesion is within the lower outer quadrant  and appears to come to within  0 lcm of the deep margin  and 0 6cm of the anterior margin  These two lesions are 1 7cm from one another  0 3cm medial to the central lesion  there is a 1 2cm cavity with a red pink granular lining located 2 5cm from the deep margin and 0 8cm from the anterior margin  1 2cm inferior to this cavity  there is a focal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm yellow granular area located  1 5cm to the closest margin  The remaining cut surface consists of white dense fibrous tissue  with multiple smooth lined cysts measuring up to 1 0cm in greatest dimension and yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No lymph nodes are identified within the lateral aspect of the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion within lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contain lesion to deep margin and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing lesion to anterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening tissue between two lesions   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains deep margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy Cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Yellow granular area and grossly uninvolved parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity  further section   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional intervening tissue between the large nodules   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of granular area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further representative section of medial breast  grossly uninvolved parenchyma   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  skin left breast   is a 4 5cm in diameter  0 3cm in thi